  "takeaways": {
    "label": "MY REFLECTION",
    "title": "TAKEAWAYS",
    "subtitle": "Understanding the Self — Personal Reflection",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Before studying Understanding the Self, I already had some understanding of who I am, but not in every aspect. I knew that I had weaknesses and things about myself that I still needed to understand and discover. One of my struggles is being shy when speaking in front of other people, which I think many students also experience.",
      "One of the lessons I enjoyed the most was learning about the different philosophies and perspectives of philosophers. I also discovered that understanding ourselves is not just about knowing our personality. There are different aspects of the self, such as the physical self, material self, and spiritual self. I wouldn't say that this subject completely changed me, but it definitely added something to my knowledge and understanding of myself.",
      "The impact of this subject on me may be small, but I still appreciate what I learned and experienced. I am not really the type of student who actively participates in recitations. Most of the time, I prefer listening and learning quietly. However, I enjoyed activities like roleplays because they gave us opportunities to express ourselves and discover our talents. I also appreciated the group quizzes because they taught us to cooperate and help one another.",
      "I am not entirely sure how I will apply everything I learned in my daily life. Maybe I am already applying some of these lessons without even realizing it. For now, I want to become a stronger, more confident person while keeping my personal life private. I also want to continue improving different aspects of myself, especially my physical health, mental well-being, and spiritual beliefs.",
      "If there is one thing I want to tell my future self, it is this: I hope you continue to understand yourself better, accept your weaknesses, and never stop growing as a person."
    ]
  }
